2026-09-08,ios,uikit,P17,ok,ok,window,default,"picker-and-sizes: re-measured. The previous coordinates (x 49/148/192/204) were all inside the empty left gutter -- P17's content is ~880 pt wide and centred in a 393 pt window -- so every row landed on nothing. The file now scrolls right and down first, and re-clamps to the bottom before its last click because a height-changing press moves everything below it. presses: LS+> and all four effects verified in p53... p17-ios-final-20260908-233736.png"
2026-09-09,ios,uikit,P9,ok,ok,window,default,"field-and-text-width: coordinates were wrong in BOTH axes -- y 541 is below the button row and x 50/122 name Narrower/Wider rather than Wider/Zero width. Re-measured to (103,479) and (175,479); 200 px -> 240 px -> 0 px, band collapses, no spill (VERIFIED p9-ios-final-20260909-002133.png). Not a defect in the app."
2026-09-09,ios,uikit,P30,ok,ok,window,default,"frame-and-effects: (28,258) is inside the blue frame rectangle, 100 pt below the button. Re-measured to (60,200); frame width 120 -> 260, button relabels, rectangle widens (VERIFIED p30-ios-final-20260908-234732.png). Not a defect in the app."
2026-09-09,ios,uikit,P34,ok,ok,window,default,"more-rows: TWO independent causes of the same silent nothing. The app must be launched with -rows 500 or both buttons are no-ops by design (rowCount and visibleRows both start at 100), and y 340 was below the button row. Re-measured to (42,295) and (173,295); 100 -> 200 -> 500 (VERIFIED p34-ios-final-20260909-003449.png for the first click alone and -003120.png for both). Not a defect in the app."
2026-09-09,macos,appkit,P54,ok,ok,window,default,refreshable: the affordance is a floating Refresh button. addSubview put it BEHIND the clip view (invisible); addFloatingSubview shows it. AppKit's origin is bottom-left so it first landed in the wrong corner. P54-press-refresh-twice.csv leaves refreshes: 2 and rows up to: 10 (VERIFIED p54-macos-final-20260909-005519.png)
2026-09-09,ios,uikit,P54,ok,ok,window,default,"refreshable: UIRefreshControl. Two things had to be fixed before a pull could reach it -- alwaysBounceVertical was false, and the control has to go on the enclosing RootScrollHost, which is the UIScrollView whose pan gesture actually wins. P54-pull-to-refresh.csv leaves refreshes: 2 and rows up to: 10 (VERIFIED p54-ios-final-20260909-013254.png)"
2026-09-09,android,android,P54,ok,ok,window,default,refreshable: a full-width Refresh row in the window's root stack. NOT inside ScrollContainer -- that Kotlin class's updateScroll is written around getChildAt(0) and a second child made the app render as a grey rectangle with Refresh in the middle and no content. P54-press-refresh-twice.csv leaves refreshes: 2 and rows up to: 10 (VERIFIED p54-android-final-20260909-015549.png)
2026-09-09,macos,appkit,P55,ok,ok,window,default,"buttonstyle isPressed: P55-press-the-styled-button.csv leaves clicks: 2 and pressed draws: 2, so a real press does reach configuration.isPressed (VERIFIED p55-macos-final-20260909-074527.png). The colour cannot be the evidence -- the button is orange only while held and a capture happens after the release"
